WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.580
Another thing Dr. Bright is not allowed to
do at the Foundation: No using SCP-159 to

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.680
make your office impenetrable!

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.089
SCP-159 is a seemingly ordinary neon sign
reading "Open."

00:00:12.089 --> 00:00:16.609
When the sign is displayed in the window of
a location, the moment it is unplugged from

00:00:16.609 --> 00:00:22.660
an electrical source it renders the building
or room impossible to enter, or destroy, using

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:25.040
anything from hurricane-level winds to X-rays.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:30.060
Dr. Bright is not allowed to borrow this sign
for his office, no matter how much he promises

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:31.849
to keep it plugged in.

00:00:31.849 --> 00:00:36.430
He does not want it for aesthetic purposes,
or, as he says, to let his colleagues know

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:37.580
they are always welcome.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:42.360
He is, in fact, planning to unplug it and
cackle wildly as anyone tries to open the

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.870
door, while yelling "You can't get me!!!"

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.850
We're not falling for that one again.

